{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/514881-new-here-question-regarding-seemings","id":514881,"title":"New here. Question regarding seemings!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-05-15T01:09:59-07:00","id":514881,"title":"New here. Question regarding seemings!","content":"Hello everyone!<br /> I've been following the Onyx Path blog for a while but there is a question who I feel I didn't get answered. I might have missed it completely though! None the less:<br /> The seemings that are being constructed for 2.0 doesn't seem to really have any seeming blessings as they did in the former version of the game. Like how ogres could spend glamour to increase the strength and how beasts get 8-again on their animal ken rolls. Is this removed and replaced by the much more powerful kith-blessings that are around now or have I just missed the information regarding seeming blessings?<br /> <br /> Thanks<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6030-a_newfie","name":"A_Newfie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-15T01:18:26-07:00","id":514900,"title":"","content":"There doesn't seem to be Seeming Blesings, but instead of that you get more bang for your buck from certain Contracs if you have a given Seeming.<br /> <br /> EDIT: for example a Contract of Strength may have different version for each Seeming, Ogres getting one that is either more potent or more widely aplicable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-15T01:54:25-07:00","id":514912,"title":"","content":"That's really cool actually! Anywhere I can read more about this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6030-a_newfie","name":"A_Newfie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-15T04:30:52-07:00","id":515038,"title":"","content":"Look for the &quot;Brainspew:Contracts&quot; thread somewhere in this same forum.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-15T07:21:32-07:00","id":515128,"title":"","content":"What Thorbes said. You might also find details on that (and some other topics) in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/385867-changeling-the-lost-second-edition-outline\">the 2e Outline</a> that Dave posted.<br /> <br /> The idea is that each Universal (i.e. non-Court and non-Goblin) Contract has the Contract itself, and then some number of Favored Seeming add-ons/modifiers/somethings. Everyone gets the Contract itself, and then everyone with one of the Favored Seemings gets that relevant add-on for free. If anyone wants the add-on for a different Favored Seeming, they can get a Changeling with that Seeming to teach it to them, at the cost of one experience. So, while the old form of Contracts as 1-5 dot progressions is going away, this seems like the replacement method for investing deeper in an area. I dig it.<br /> <br /> As a caveat, it <i>is</i> possible that Seemings may have more to them than we've yet seen, or Dave and Filamina might later decide they should. Just that at the moment, the Clarity-oriented Curses and Blessings, plus Contract affinities, are all we know for sure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}